'''''Survivor 51''''' is the ongoing 51st season of the American competitive reality television series [[Survivor (American TV series)|''Survivor'']]. It premiered on September 23, 2026<ref name=":0" /> on [[CBS]] in the [[United States]]. It was the 19th consecutive season to be filmed in the [[Mamanuca Islands]] in [[Fiji]].

==Format==
{{Main|Survivor (American TV series)#Format and rules}}
''[[Survivor (American TV series)|Survivor]]'' is a [[reality television]] show based on the Swedish show ''[[Expedition Robinson]]'', created by [[Mark Burnett]] and [[Charlie Parsons]].<ref name="avclub history">{{cite web |url=https://www.avclub.com/article/survivors-first-alliance-changed-gameand-reality-t-236577 |title=Survivor's first "alliance" changed the game—and reality TV |first=Noel |last=Murray |date=May 17, 2016 |access-date=May 17, 2016 |work=[[The A.V. Club]] |archive-date=May 18, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160518094236/http://www.avclub.com/article/survivors-first-alliance-changed-gameand-reality-t-236577 |url-status=live}}</ref> The series follows a number of participants isolated in a remote location, where they must provide food, fire, and shelter.<ref name="avclub history"/> One by one, a participant is removed from the series by majority vote, with challenges held to give a reward (ranging from living- and food-related prizes to a car) and immunity from being voted out of the series.<ref name=rules>{{Cite book |title=The Psychology of Survivor - Google Books |isbn=9781935251385 |pages=2–11 |publisher=BenBella Books |date=July 11, 2007 |access-date=December 30, 2021 |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=FdrILXwh7nEC |archive-date=December 31, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211231095031/https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/The_Psychology_of_Survivor/FdrILXwh7nEC?hl=en&gbpv=0 |url-status=live }}</ref> The last remaining player receives a prize of $1,000,000.<ref name=rules/>

==Contestants==
The 21 castaways were officially announced on August 25, 2026. This is the first ''Survivor'' season to start with an odd number of castaways since ''[[Survivor: Fiji]]'' in 2007, the first season whose opening cast had a female majority (eleven women and ten men), and the first to start with a gender imbalance since ''[[Survivor: San Juan del Sur]]'' (which had ten men and eight women). Notable cast members this season include actor [[Devin Way]], voice actress [[Ana Sani]], and former [[NXT (WWE brand)|WWE NXT]] wrestler Brady Booker.<ref name="parade">{{cite magazine|url=https://parade.com/tv/survivor-51-cast-2026 |title=''Survivor 51'' Cast Revealed: Meet the 21 New Contestants — Including a Former WWE Superstar and ''Grey’s Anatomy'' Star|magazine=Parade|last=Bloom|first=Mike|date=August 26, 2026|access-date=August 26, 2026}}</ref><ref name="EW">{{cite magazine|url=https://ew.com/survivor-51-cast-revealed-12068720 |title=Meet the cast of ''Survivor 51''|magazine=Entertainment Weekly|last=Ross|first=Dalton|date=August 26, 2026|access-date=August 26, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Currier |first=Joseph |date=2026-05-20 |title=Former WWE NXT wrestler reportedly cast on 'Survivor 51' |url=https://www.f4wonline.com/news/aew/brady-booker-reportedly-cast-on-survivor-51/ |access-date=2026-08-31 |website=F4W/WON |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref name="Variety">{{cite magazine |last=Hailu |first=Selome |date=August 26, 2026 |title=''Survivor 51'': Meet the 21 New Castaways, Including a ''Grey’s Anatomy'' Actor, the Voice of Strawberry Shortcake, a Pro Wrestler and a Yankees Exec |url=https://variety.com/lists/survivor-51-cast-greys-anatomy-strawberry-shortcake/ |access-date=September 21, 2026 |magazine=Variety}}</ref> 

