| ShortSummary    = Returning to camp, Brady and his alliance are hurt and upset by Patt's blindside. They search for answers about the vote flip, while the others quietly celebrate taking down the larger alliance. On Day 8, Jeff announces a tribe swap that will divide the remaining castaways into three tribes. Alexis, Devin, Jelly, Jenna and Ori join Savu; Brady, Carter, Kristin, Maggie, Mike and Thien An join Toka; and Cristian, Eric, Kilby, Lewis, Linnea and Sharonda form the new Dina tribe.

At Dina, the tribe must start from scratch by building a new camp. Kilby and Eric bond over their difficult starts on their previous tribes, while Lewis struggles with feeling sick and tired. At the new Toka beach, Kristin works to get to know her new tribemates as the only newcomer to the group. She also attempts to smooth things over with Carter following his mutiny. Carter and Thien An secretly form an alliance with hopes of reaching the end together. At Savu, Jenna attempts to smooth things over with Devin, hoping they can remain loyal to original Toka and vote out Alexis or Ori. Meanwhile, sparks fly between Jelly and Ori.

*'''Reward/Immunity Challenge:''' One tribe member closest to the ocean must collect a bucket of water. They then have to work with their tribe to pass the water to each other by throwing it in the air and catching it in their buckets, with the final member eventually dumping the remaining water into a container which, when filled, would drop and release a ball. Two tribe members must then use the ball to complete a circular maze. The first two tribes to finish wins immunity and a full ''Survivor'' coffee kit for first place and a jar of iced coffee for second place.

The new Dina tribe finishes first, with Toka coming in second and sending Savu to Tribal Council. Back at camp, Alexis attempts to secure her safety by convincing Ori to vote out either Jelly or Devin, unaware of the Helicopter Alliance between the three. However, Devin continues to view Jenna as the better target over Alexis, while Jelly believes the opposite. At Tribal Council, Jenna is ultimately voted out in a 4–1 vote.
